# CODEOWNERS — Thot Secure
#
# Path ownership for automatic review requests on pull requests.
# Syntax: <pattern> <owner>...   ('*' is a glob, '!' negates, last match wins)
#
# Owners are GitHub *teams*, never individuals, so that a person can join or
# leave a role without rewriting path rules: @thotsecure/core, @thotsecure/detection,
# @thotsecure/actions, @thotsecure/docs, @thotsecure/security.
#
# Rules of thumb used below:
#   * the default owner is @thotsecure/core, so every new file has a reviewer;
#   * security-sensitive paths (auth, tenancy, audit, crypto, CI credentials,
#     signing) always pull in @thotsecure/security, which is a blocking review;
#   * paths are listed from broad to specific, because the last matching
#     pattern wins;
#   * ROADMAP.md and MAINTAINERS.md list the areas each team covers.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Default: anything not matched below belongs to the core team.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*                                       @thotsecure/core

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Governance, legal and repository-level policy
# (changing these changes the project's guarantees, not just its code)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/LICENSE                                @thotsecure/core @thotsecure/security
/NOTICE                                 @thotsecure/core @thotsecure/security
/GOVERNANCE.md                          @thotsecure/core @thotsecure/security
/MAINTAINERS.md                         @thotsecure/core
/SECURITY.md                            @thotsecure/security
/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md                     @thotsecure/core @thotsecure/security
/CONTRIBUTING.md                        @thotsecure/docs @thotsecure/core
/CITATION.cff                           @thotsecure/docs
/CHANGELOG.md                           @thotsecure/core
/ROADMAP.md                             @thotsecure/core
/CODEOWNERS                             @thotsecure/core @thotsecure/security
/README.md                              @thotsecure/docs
/pyproject.toml                         @thotsecure/core
/Makefile                               @thotsecure/core
/mkdocs.yml                             @thotsecure/docs
/.editorconfig                          @thotsecure/core
/.gitattributes                         @thotsecure/core
/.gitignore                             @thotsecure/core
/.pre-commit-config.yaml                @thotsecure/core
/.yamllint                              @thotsecure/core

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Application package — src/thotsecure/ (see api-contract.md §2)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/src/thotsecure/core/                     @thotsecure/core
/src/thotsecure/storage/                  @thotsecure/core
/src/thotsecure/bus/                      @thotsecure/core
/src/thotsecure/reports/                  @thotsecure/core
/src/thotsecure/sdk/                      @thotsecure/core
/src/thotsecure/cli.py                    @thotsecure/core

# Audit chain and tenant isolation: an invariant, and the most security-critical
# code in the repository (api-contract.md §10).
/src/thotsecure/audit/                    @thotsecure/security
/src/thotsecure/tenancy/                  @thotsecure/security @thotsecure/core

# API surface: authentication, RBAC and capability checks live here.
/src/thotsecure/api/                      @thotsecure/core @thotsecure/security

# Detection pipeline and the telemetry it consumes.
/src/thotsecure/detection/                @thotsecure/detection
/src/thotsecure/scoring/                  @thotsecure/detection
/src/thotsecure/collectors/               @thotsecure/detection @thotsecure/security

# Decision, execution and rollback.
/src/thotsecure/decision/                 @thotsecure/actions @thotsecure/security
/src/thotsecure/actions/                  @thotsecure/actions @thotsecure/security

# Embedded console (Jinja2 + JS, no Node build) — XSS surface.
/src/thotsecure/ui/                       @thotsecure/docs @thotsecure/security

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Declarative content shipped with the product
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
